{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106569","id":2527095668,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6WoGt0","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106569","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106569.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106569.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106569","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106569/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106569/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106569/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/6fe17b264e149169da057a20ffdd585bd837617b","number":106569,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Accelerate `HashMap` and `HashSet` lookup by using `if` based modulo in loops","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`HashMap` uses modulo to map hashes and positions to the `0 to capacity` range.\r\nModulo is slow, so it was exchanged for `fastmod` in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/62327.\r\nHowever, `fastmod` is still a bottleneck for `HashMap` lookup. I was able to accelerate calls by using an `if` pseudo modulo instead, which is faster than `fastmod`.\r\n\r\nThis change can accelerate `HashMap` lookup by 40%.\r\n\r\n## Explanation\r\n\r\nOn my machine, `fastmod` uses 2 multiplications (3-10 clock cycles[^2] each) and a bitshift (1 clock cycle[^3]). \r\n\r\nAn `if` is an integer comparison (1 clock cycle[^3]) and a mostly predictable branch (0-2 clock cycles[^1] normally, 12 - 25 clock cycles on modulo case). \r\n\r\nIt stands to reason that in most cases, an `if` based modulo will be faster than `fastmod`. It can be used when we're sure the number is between `(0, capacity * 2 - 1)`.\r\n\r\n## Benchmarks\r\n\r\nTheory is well and good, but benchmarks are better. \r\nI measured an up to 40% improvement in `HashMap` `get`, 11% for `insert`, and 2.5% for `erase`.\r\nThis will be the case notably mostly when the memory is in cache. When it is not in cache, the bottleneck is likely to be RAM access.\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Test Code</summary>\r\n\r\n```c++\r\n\tfor (int size : { 1, 2, 8, 64, 1024, 4096}) {\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tsize_t time_ns = 0;\r\n\t\t\tfor (int run = 0; run < 20000000 / size; run++) {\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\t\t\tHashMap<int64_t, int64_t> dictionary;\r\n\t\t\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < size; idx ++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\t\t\tdictionary.insert(idx, idx);\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\t\t\ttime_ns += std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::nanoseconds>(t1 - t0).count();\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << \"insert:\" << size << std::endl;\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << time_ns / 1000 / 1000 << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tsize_t time_ns = 0;\r\n\t\t\tfor (int run = 0; run < 20000000 / size; run++) {\r\n\t\t\t\tHashMap<int64_t, int64_t> dictionary;\r\n\t\t\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < size; idx ++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\t\t\tdictionary.insert(idx, idx);\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\t\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < size; idx ++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\t\t\tdictionary.erase(idx);\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\t\t\ttime_ns += std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::nanoseconds>(t1 - t0).count();\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << \"erase:\" << size << std::endl;\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << time_ns / 1000 / 1000 << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tsize_t time_ns = 0;\r\n\t\t\tfor (int run = 0; run < 20000000 / size; run++) {\r\n\t\t\t\tHashMap<int64_t, int64_t> dictionary;\r\n\t\t\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < size; idx ++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\t\t\tdictionary.insert(idx, idx);\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\tsize_t total = 0;\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\t\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < size; idx ++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\t\t\ttotal += dictionary.get(idx);\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\t\t\ttime_ns += std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::nanoseconds>(t1 - t0).count();\r\n\r\n\t\t\t\t// Prevent compiling this out.\r\n\t\t\t\tvolatile_size_t = total;\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << \"get:\" << size << std::endl;\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << time_ns / 1000 / 1000 << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nOn master:\r\n```\r\ninsert:1\r\n912ms\r\nerase:1\r\n522ms\r\nget:1\r\n330ms\r\ninsert:2\r\n552ms\r\nerase:2\r\n383ms\r\nget:2\r\n174ms\r\ninsert:8\r\n310ms\r\nerase:8\r\n376ms\r\nget:8\r\n86ms\r\ninsert:64\r\n406ms\r\nerase:64\r\n462ms\r\nget:64\r\n98ms\r\ninsert:1024\r\n511ms\r\nerase:1024\r\n587ms\r\nget:1024\r\n105ms\r\ninsert:4096\r\n861ms\r\nerase:4096\r\n643ms\r\nget:4096\r\n272ms\r\n```\r\n\r\nOn this PR:\r\n```\r\ninsert:1\r\n913ms\r\nerase:1\r\n521ms\r\nget:1\r\n321ms\r\ninsert:2\r\n544ms\r\nerase:2\r\n376ms\r\nget:2\r\n164ms\r\ninsert:8\r\n292ms\r\nerase:8\r\n371ms\r\nget:8\r\n61ms\r\ninsert:64\r\n376ms\r\nerase:64\r\n459ms\r\nget:64\r\n65ms\r\ninsert:1024\r\n475ms\r\nerase:1024\r\n565ms\r\nget:1024\r\n64ms\r\ninsert:4096\r\n769ms\r\nerase:4096\r\n627ms\r\nget:4096\r\n190ms\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Alternatives\r\n\r\n@nazarwadim has proposed in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/90082 to switch to `&` for modulus. This would make the operation near instantaneous. \r\n\r\nHowever, we currently use prime based capacities, because those decrease collision counts when a mediocre hash strategy is chosen. There is definitely a trade off to be measured some time, but it should be measured with both strategies at an ideal implementation.\r\n\r\nSince we know our hash functions are high quality, this may be a better solution in the end. Using power of two growth seems to make for a better trade-off in most modern `HashMap` implementations anyway. I will likely test this soon.\r\nJava apparently applies a secondary hash function to the given hash, to increase quality (https://stackoverflow.com/a/15437377/730797). We could always use that for unknown hash functions (and not do it for known, high quality hash functions).\r\n\r\n[^1]: https://agner.org/optimize/optimizing_cpp.pdf p. 43\r\n[^2]: https://agner.org/optimize/optimizing_cpp.pdf p. 149\r\n[^3]: https://agner.org/optimize/optimizing_cpp.pdf p. 30","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/22","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22/labels","number":22,"state":"closed","title":"4.5","description":"","creator":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauermann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":3687,"created_at":"2024-12-19T08:51:28Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T21:48:38Z","closed_at":"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z","due_on":"2025-09-15T00:00:00Z"},"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-05-18T18:05:57Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T14:53:21Z","closed_at":"2025-05-27T14:50:36Z","merged_at":"2025-05-27T14:50:36Z","merge_commit_sha":"0c12e758ac5e16a704ff4fe14dcd392b1b159f1b","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[]